## ✅ Implementation Checklist for Rider App

Apply these patterns to your rider app:

- [ ] Replace any existing location package with `geolocator: ^10.1.0`
- [ ] Implement permission checking at multiple stages
- [ ] Add 10-second timeout to all `getCurrentPosition()` calls
- [ ] Implement [_tryLastKnownPosition()](file:///d:/coding-repo/taxi-app/taxi_driver_app/lib/providers/location_provider.dart#103-121) fallback
- [ ] Handle all exception types (Timeout, ServiceDisabled, PermissionDenied)
- [ ] Add proper Android manifest permissions
- [ ] Add proper iOS Info.plist descriptions
- [ ] Use `LocationSettings` with `distanceFilter: 10`
- [ ] Test in all scenarios:
  - [ ] GPS disabled
  - [ ] Permissions denied
  - [ ] Slow GPS signal
  - [ ] Indoor location
  - [ ] App in background
  - [ ] App killed and reopened

---

## 🎯 Why This Strategy Works

| Pattern | Benefit |
|---------|---------|
| **Timeout Protection** | Prevents app from hanging when GPS is slow |
| **Last Known Fallback** | Always has a location, even if fresh GPS fails |
| **Multiple Permission Checks** | Handles permission changes during app lifecycle |
| **Service Availability Check** | Detects when location services are disabled |
| **Specific Exception Handling** | Handles each failure scenario appropriately |
| **Distance Filter** | Reduces battery drain and unnecessary updates |
| **Async Initialization** | Doesn't block app startup |

---

## 🚀 Quick Start for Rider App

1. **Copy the LocationProvider template** above into your rider app
2. **Update [pubspec.yaml](file:///d:/coding-repo/taxi-app/taxi_driver_app/pubspec.yaml)** with the dependencies
3. **Add platform permissions** (Android manifest + iOS Info.plist)
4. **Initialize in main.dart**:

```dart
void main() {
  runApp(
    MultiProvider(
      providers: [
        ChangeNotifierProvider(create: (_) => LocationProvider()),
        // ... other providers
      ],
      child: MyApp(),
    ),
  );
}
```

5. **Use in your widgets**:

```dart
final locationProvider = Provider.of<LocationProvider>(context);
final position = locationProvider.currentPosition;

if (position != null) {
  // Use position.latitude and position.longitude
}
```

